<title>POLAND: Boeing team offers Poland combat avionics.</title>
<headline>Boeing team offers Poland combat avionics.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of Western firms led by Boeing Co is touring Poland to present proposals for participation in the $850 million production programme of the Polish Huzar combat helicopter, the group said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the 25-firm group included Britain's GEC-Marconi, Sweden's Saab, Italy's Finmeccanica, as well as Rockwell-Collins, Fairchild Defence, United Technologies Corp unit Pratt &amp; Whitney and Pilkington Optronics.</p>
<p>&quot;In line with the Polish government requirements, the Boeing team is committed to offsetting 100 percent of the Huzar programme costs through industrial projects in Poland,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The group, which hopes to be chosen by the Polish government to provide avionics and an integration package for the Huzar helicopter, plans to visit defence and aviation factories in the towns of Swidnik, Mielec, Rzeszow and Tarnow.</p>
<p>Poland is developing its Sokol helicopter into the combat Huzar made by the domestic firm PZL Swidnik, and aims gradually to provide its own armed forces with 150 of them.</p>
<p>(( -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 ))</p>
